{"id":"c045448153929107","group":"73","path":"73/73-thm-epsilon-transition-elimination.md","title":"NFA–Epsilon-NFA Language Equivalence","display":"thm-nfa-epsilon-nfa-equivalence — NFA–Epsilon-NFA Language Equivalence","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Automata Theory, Languages and Computation (Hopcroft, Ullman)","book_abbrev":"73","label":"73-thm-epsilon-transition-elimination","aliases":["73-thm-epsilon-transition-elimination","73-thm-nfa-epsilon-nfa-equivalence"],"display":"thm-nfa-epsilon-nfa-equivalence — NFA–Epsilon-NFA Language Equivalence","depends_on":["[[73-df-epsilon-reachability]]","[[73-df-epsilon-nfa-language-semantics]]","[[73-df-nfa-language-semantics]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Automata Theory, Languages and Computation (Hopcroft, Ullman)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"73"},{"key":"label","html":"73-thm-epsilon-transition-elimination"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>73-thm-epsilon-transition-elimination</span><span>73-thm-nfa-epsilon-nfa-equivalence</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-nfa-epsilon-nfa-equivalence — NFA–Epsilon-NFA Language Equivalence"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"f4625243fc1dd8f0\" href=\"?note=f4625243fc1dd8f0\" title=\"73-df-epsilon-reachability\">73-df-epsilon-reachability</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"b4ab199feb1a8020\" href=\"?note=b4ab199feb1a8020\" title=\"73-df-epsilon-nfa-language-semantics\">73-df-epsilon-nfa-language-semantics</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"1d700ea676b35b73\" href=\"?note=1d700ea676b35b73\" title=\"73-df-nfa-language-semantics\">73-df-nfa-language-semantics</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span> (alphabet)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma},\\mathsf{ENFA}_{\\Sigma}\">\\(\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma},\\mathsf{ENFA}_{\\Sigma}\\)</span> and their accepted-language maps</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{EClos}\">\\(\\operatorname{EClos}\\)</span> (epsilon closure, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"f4625243fc1dd8f0\" href=\"?note=f4625243fc1dd8f0\" title=\"73-df-epsilon-reachability\">73-df-epsilon-reachability</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}nfa\\text{-}epsilon\\text{-}nfa\\text{-}equivalence}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\left[\n\\exists E\\in\\mathsf{ENFA}_{\\Sigma}\\;(L=L(E))\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists N\\in\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma}\\;(L=L(N))\n\\right]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}nfa\\text{-}epsilon\\text{-}nfa\\text{-}equivalence}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\left[\n\\exists E\\in\\mathsf{ENFA}_{\\Sigma}\\;(L=L(E))\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists N\\in\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma}\\;(L=L(N))\n\\right]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Eliminate epsilon moves by setting\n<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\delta&#39;(q,a)=\\operatorname{EClos}(\\bigcup_{p\\in\\operatorname{EClos}(q)}\\delta(p,a))\">\\(\\delta&#39;(q,a)=\\operatorname{EClos}(\\bigcup_{p\\in\\operatorname{EClos}(q)}\\delta(p,a))\\)</span>\nand <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F&#39;=\\{q:\\operatorname{EClos}(q)\\cap F\\neq\\varnothing\\}\">\\(F&#39;=\\{q:\\operatorname{EClos}(q)\\cap F\\neq\\varnothing\\}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The reverse direction assigns the empty set to every epsilon transition. Induction on input length proves both constructions preserve the language.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"73-df-epsilon-reachability","status":"resolved","id":"f4625243fc1dd8f0","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-epsilon-reachability]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-epsilon-nfa-language-semantics","status":"resolved","id":"b4ab199feb1a8020","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-epsilon-nfa-language-semantics]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-nfa-language-semantics","status":"resolved","id":"1d700ea676b35b73","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-nfa-language-semantics]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-epsilon-reachability","status":"resolved","id":"f4625243fc1dd8f0","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{EClos}$ (epsilon closure, see [[73-df-epsilon-reachability]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\Sigma","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma},\\mathsf{ENFA}_{\\Sigma}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{EClos}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}nfa\\text{-}epsilon\\text{-}nfa\\text{-}equivalence}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\left[\n\\exists E\\in\\mathsf{ENFA}_{\\Sigma}\\;(L=L(E))\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists N\\in\\mathsf{NFA}_{\\Sigma}\\;(L=L(N))\n\\right]","display":true},{"tex":"\\delta'(q,a)=\\operatorname{EClos}(\\bigcup_{p\\in\\operatorname{EClos}(q)}\\delta(p,a))","display":false},{"tex":"F'=\\{q:\\operatorname{EClos}(q)\\cap F\\neq\\varnothing\\}","display":false}],"bytes":1327,"backlinks":[{"id":"a2d140de13ec8897","anchor":"ref-10","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"5a5b99309397a57a","anchor":"ref-5","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"fa5a4ce6b6982a00","anchor":"ref-7","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"Thompson's structural construction maps each regular expression to an equivalent epsilon-NFA; [[73-thm-epsilon-transition-elimination]] and [[73-thm-nfa-determinization]] then give a DFA."}],"outgoing":["f4625243fc1dd8f0","b4ab199feb1a8020","1d700ea676b35b73"]}